  "notes": "Describes a state of heightened emotional arousal. Can be positive (excitement, thrill) or negative (agitation, being worked up). The noun form {興奮|こうふん} is also very common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {興奮|こうふん}が{冷|さ}める: the excitement dies down\n- {興奮|こうふん}{状態|じょうたい}: state of excitement\n- {興奮|こうふん}{気味|ぎみ}: somewhat excited\n- {興奮|こうふん}を{抑|おさ}える: to suppress one's excitement\n- {大|おお}{興奮|こうふん}: great excitement\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ワクワクする: to be thrilled — implies pleasant anticipation, always positive\n- ドキドキする: heart pounding — implies nervousness or excitement, often romantic\n- {昂|たかぶ}る: to be worked up — literary, emphasizes rising emotions",
